! Step 18 hand-back

Head `19048159c1c5beec52f72c049e5c53dc20cb6779`; state counter stays 18; no live seats, commit, or push. Next unused relay request: 035. Requests 032–034 resolved. LIVENESS: the receipt helper's 120-second timeout names a broker that may have died; no timeout occurred this step.

The uncommitted daemon-side fleet watcher follows the seat's own Repo board in `operator-daemon-behavior.ts`, shared by browser and node. It subscribes before waking on initial attachment, signals `daemonChanged` and wakes the seat on changes, and detaches on veil disposal; a stop during open does not attach. Request 032 ran the new single file red (2 failures: missing watcher). Request 033 passed the initial 2 tests; request 034 passed all 3, including a board lift that overtakes a standing read and an unchanged-aside control. `git diff --check` passes. The earlier ring callback and its test remain uncommitted and without a consumer.

This does NOT establish end-to-end browser or node transport or close ingest TOCTOU: tests exercise the extracted watcher and seat together using a fake handle, not live vessel composition. The watcher retries no rejected board open after logging; prove/rework lifecycle recovery, initial attachment, changes during actual board refold, and local replica behavior in both vessels. Its change callback invalidates the seat's proof version, but `absorbCapEvents` may mutate the Keyhive before an await returns: add a guarded or serialized commit boundary and a red with control that actually exercises authority mutation. A post-await version check cannot cure this. `onRefold` may fire after rejection, so it cannot certify publication. The currently unused ring callback should be removed if direct local observation proves sufficient, or wired safely if needed.

Founder lineage freshness and tri-state ring, slice-1 blind-read residues and daemon join TOCTOU, independently complete dyad census (fleet board has no roster), and `runApplyAdmitPayload`, holder-session-proof and leaf-peer-proof remain owed. Preserve roll guard and epoch fields. Run daemon tests as broker named single files with prescribed sandbox; run whole non-daemon suites before ready; e2e stays in CI. Obtain blind Opus custody read before land; no push without controller go.

